      "content": "To calculate the straight-line depreciation, first you determine the depreciable base by subtracting the salvage value from the original cost ($145,000 - $15,000 = $130,000). Next, you divide this depreciable base by the estimated useful life (8 years) to find the annual depreciation expense. Therefore, the annual depreciation expense for your CNC milling machine is $16,250 ($130,000 / 8). This consistent annual charge will allow you to accurately track depreciation for your financial statements.",
      "source": "target",
